      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have another idea for gesture ANIMATIONS. To make the life easier for VRC developer, why not make use of the current gesture system? Player may \"active\" the ANIMATION by doing the same gesture of the override. For example, when the player do a \"finger point\" gesture in real life, it activate \"finger point override\" animation. When the player's gesture doesn't active any override, the avatar should just reflect the real player's finger position. This should be easier to implement and feel more natural.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
